<div data-schema-only="false" class="wp-block-aioseo-faq"><h3 class="aioseo-faq-block-question">What is lossless image compression?</h3><div class="aioseo-faq-block-answer">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Lossless image compression shrinks files but allows perfect reconstruction of the original. It&#8217;s ideal for graphics needing sharp edges. Many free online image tools offer this for images for free.</p>
</div></div>



<div data-schema-only="false" class="wp-block-aioseo-faq"><h3 class="aioseo-faq-block-question">How does JPG image compression work?</h3><div class="aioseo-faq-block-answer">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">JPG relies on lossy compression with discrete cosine transform to group similar colors. It discards subtle variations humans rarely spot. We frequently compress JPG files for WooCommerce product galleries.</p>
</div></div>



<div data-schema-only="false" class="wp-block-aioseo-faq"><h3 class="aioseo-faq-block-question">How does PNG image compression work?</h3><div class="aioseo-faq-block-answer">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">PNG file compression uses lossless methods to deflate data patterns without quality loss. It supports transparency and works great for logos. An online optimizer handles PNG files efficiently.</p>
</div></div>



<div data-schema-only="false" class="wp-block-aioseo-faq"><h3 class="aioseo-faq-block-question">Why should I compress my images for my website?</h3><div class="aioseo-faq-block-answer">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Compressed images speed up page loads and improve user experience across devices. They also help SEO rankings and cut hosting costs. Every site I&#8217;ve optimized saw better performance after proper image optimization.</p>
</div></div>



<div data-schema-only="false" class="wp-block-aioseo-faq"><h3 class="aioseo-faq-block-question">Does image compression reduce quality?</h3><div class="aioseo-faq-block-answer">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">It can, especially with aggressive lossy settings, but smart choices minimize visible impact. Convert images wisely and test results. Good tools let you compress an image while keeping it sharp.</p>
</div></div>



<div data-schema-only="false" class="wp-block-aioseo-faq"><h3 class="aioseo-faq-block-question">What are the two types of image compression?</h3><div class="aioseo-faq-block-answer">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The two types are lossy and lossless. Lossy creates smaller files with some data removal, while lossless preserves everything. We pick based on file types like GIF and PNG or photos.</p>
</div></div>
