<p class="wp-block-paragraph">A WordPress hacked site frequently shows there has been a critical error on this website wordpress because malicious code interferes with normal operation. Hackers inject files that trigger the error or overload the server.&nbsp;You might also discover attempts to prevent unauthorized access to media files in WordPress were bypassed, leaving sensitive areas exposed. Checking WordPress error logs reveals suspicious activity. Cleaning malware requires removing bad code and strengthening security right away.</p>



